        "title": "Yarn and Spinning",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SAXONY WHEEL (Treadle Wheel, ~1480 CE):\n    Treadle (foot pedal) → crank → drive wheel\n    Flyer and bobbin mechanism: CONTINUOUS spinning\n    Flyer adds twist; bobbin takes up yarn simultaneously\n    Both hands free for drafting\n    Speed: ~5-10× drop spindle\n    This is the archetypal \"spinning wheel\" in fairy tales"
    },
    {
