      "text": "WATER FRAME (Arkwright, 1769):\n  Roller drafting (not hand drafting)\n  Rollers moving at different speeds stretch the roving\n  Water-powered (required factory installation)\n  Produced STRONGER, harder-twisted yarn than jenny\n  (suitable for warp thread — jenny yarn too soft for warp)\n  This is why Arkwright built factories: scale + water power\n  Patent fights: Arkwright's monopoly bitterly contested"
    }
